<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Rain halts Texas harvest again.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Rain halts Texas harvest again.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heavy rains moved across central Texas Friday morning, further delaying the hard red winter wheat harvest, grain merchandisers said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's raining right now in Abilene. There are flash flood warnings in Runnels County,&quot; a Fort Worth, Texas, merchandiser said at 0845 CDT.</p>
<p>Cool, wet weather has delayed the harvest across much of Texas by two weeks, causing basis levels and futures prices to stay firm.</p>
<p>Basis levels Friday were mostly steady Friday, although some weakness was reported at Kansas locations.  </p>
